Handle GetVolumePathNamesForVolumeName() failure in getmntent().
getmntent() calls GetVolumePathNamesForVolumeName() once to size the
list of a volume's mount points and again to fill it, and checked
neither call. If the first failed with anything but ERROR_MORE_DATA,
for instance because the volume went away, the size stayed 0, and
getmntent() read the first byte of a zero-sized allocation (or, if
malloc(0) returned NULL, dereferenced NULL); if the second failed, it
walked an uninitialised buffer. Allocate one spare byte, and treat a
failed call as an empty list, so the volume is skipped.

---
 win32/mntent.c |    7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/win32/mntent.c
+++ b/win32/mntent.c
@@ -129,9 +129,10 @@
 		/* Mount point list is a single string array which may contain
 		 * many items separated by NUL, terminated by two NULs */
 		GetVolumePathNamesForVolumeName(state->vol_name, NULL, 0, &need);
-		state->mount_list = state->mount_ptr = xmalloc(need);
-		GetVolumePathNamesForVolumeName(state->vol_name, state->mount_list,
-											need, &need);
+		state->mount_list = state->mount_ptr = xmalloc(need + 1);
+		if (!GetVolumePathNamesForVolumeName(state->vol_name,
+					state->mount_list, need, &need))
+			state->mount_ptr[0] = '\0';
 		if (state->mount_ptr[0] == '\0')
 			goto next_vol;
 	}
